Commands:
cd - change dirctory
syntax: cd folder_name
eg: cd javalearning
====================================================
cd .. (double dot):
      It goes to the previous previos folder
Eg:  C:\Users\YourUsername\Documents>cd ..
     C:\Users\YourUsername
=====================================================
cd ..\.. (double dot backward slash double dot):
      It goes to the two previous folders
Eg:   C:\Users\YourUsername\Documents>cd ..\..
      C:\Users>
======================================================
tab key:
      Pressing tab key gives the available 
folders or files in a folder
=====================================================================     
dir command:
     This command shows all the files and folders in a folder
Eg:
      dir C:\Windows

    To display the hidden files in a folder
Eg:   dir /a

    To display the file according to their size.
Eg:   dir /o:s

    To display the files according to their alphabetical order.
Eg:   dir /o:n

    To display what a specific type of files(particular extension)
Eg:   dir *.txt -> shows all the text files
      dir *.png -> shows all the png files
